---
import MarketingLayout from '../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
---

<MarketingLayout title="Privacy" description="Privacy notes for Cove and the public website.">
  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow-small">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="page-heading">Your data stays on your system</h1>
      <p class="page-copy">Cove does not include telemetry and does not send your library data to Cove servers. The app runs where you install it, and you decide which external metadata providers, downloaders, reverse proxies, or integrations to use.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marketing-section">
    <div class="marketing-section-inner info-grid">
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Cove app</h3><p>No telemetry. Your library, generated media, metadata, users, roles, and permissions remain on the system running Cove.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>External services</h3><p>Cove only contacts external metadata, scraper, downloader, or AI services when you configure and use workflows that require them.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>This website</h3><p>The public docs site is a static GitHub Pages site and does not add first-party analytics.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
